From daabf3c6926f2ec5c47b3b3cef5d16c051f0340b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robbi <ropebe51@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 23:30:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Helios Requiem polish pass 2: hunt, escalate, smooth,
 star vault

A  Herald: new Starfall (leap into the star's light, hunt a player with a
   floor ring, lock, meteor dive + jumpable shockwave; 2x below 50 %),
   84 BPM, moves chain on the next beat, flurries 3/4, 4-beat openings that
   start as soon as his move ends, one hazard alongside his own move.
   Blink vanishes in place, streak + lunge + follow-through. Body pushed
   every tick with interpolation overlap; blade double-push fixed; mirror
   shuffle/reveal are cuts; intro blades visible; English title.
B  Star: accumulated spin phase (spin changes made the whole star and belt
   jump), eased spin, odd-tick pushes, 3-tick interpolation at 2-tick
   cadence (also rig, debris, singularity, falling sectors, supernova).
C  Constellation: after the relay the floor beam HUNTS (weighty chase,
   retargets every 2 beats with ping + hairline), then the scar TEARS
   (fuses, chained eruptions, holes that grow back). Requiem keeps the
   short form. Portal spin no longer jumps.
E  Singularity: Helios herds from outside the party; new Gravity Tether
   binds a player to the hole (extra pull, one burn, Helios holds the rein).
F  Supernova: unstable-star convulsions with metal/glass crashes and sky
   strobe, second wall + roar + sky fractures + aftershocks after the blast.
G  Star Vault born out of the dying star, floats over the pit, builds a
   dais and four N/E/S/W staircases beat by beat; capsules come out of it
   onto the dais. Loot wiring unchanged. Cleared on every exit.

helios.yml v4 (new knobs: herald.starfall, herald.pacing, portals hunt/tear,
helios.tether). D (arena expansion) intentionally left out: see
BossEngine/docs/HELIOS_POLISH_PASS2_CHANGELOG.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
